policy (say, NAFTA), that doesn't necessarily mean that it maximizes
the economic good of all classes of people (say, UAW workers).  Those
classes, if they understand the situation and can organize and obtain
political power, will quite rationally oppose the policy.  I think one
could construct perverse examples where the *majority* of the
population could lose income from a market-freeing policy.  (But, of
course, the *mean* income would rise.)

